le's year?</h3></div><span class="transition-transform duration-300 ease-out flex items-center ml-auto"><i class="icon-chevron-down flex justify-center items-center icon-md " aria-hidden="true" data-qa-id="accordion-summary-_r_e_-how-do-i-find-my-vehicle's-year?-2-icon-chevron" style="font-size: 24px; width: 24px; height: 24px; color: currentcolor;"><span class="path1"></span><span class="path2"></span><span class="path3"></span><span class="path4"></span><span class="path5"></span><span class="path6"></span><span class="path7"></span><span class="path8"></span><span class="path9"></span><span class="path10"></span><span class="path11"></span><span class="path12"></span><span class="path13"></span><span class="path14"></span></i></span></button><div id="accordion-content-_r_e_-how-do-i-find-my-vehicle's-year?-2" role="region" aria-labelledby="accordion-header-_r_e_-how-do-i-find-my-vehicle's-year?-2" class="overflow-hidden transition-[height] duration-300 ease-in pb-0 px-0 pb-6" aria-hidden="true" data-qa-id="accordion-details-_r_e_-how-do-i-find-my-vehicle's-year?-2" style="overflow: hidden; transition: height 0.3s; display: none; height: 0px;"><div class="flex flex-col gap-4"><div class="text-black last:mb-0"><p class="paragraph-md text-action-color-secondary !normal-case">Knowing your vehicle's year of manufacturing is absolutely critical for selecting the right tires. You'll find it on a sticker inside the driver's side door jamb, within your VIN (Vehicle Identification Number), or on your vehicle's title or registration.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="border-t-2 last:border-b-2 text-type-standard  border-background-100 border-background-100" data-open="false" data-qa-id="accordion-item-_r_e_-what-is-a-vehicle-model-and-how-can-i-find-it?-3"><button aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="accordion-content-_r_e_-what-is-a-vehicle-model-and-how-can-i-find-it?-3" id="accordion-header-_r_e_-what-is-a-vehicle-model-and-how-can-i-find-it?-3" class="py-4 pr-6 pl-